without the rule, the highest vase sits at 1100 mm
with a 400mm limit, vases sit at ["0","200"] and 0 were left behind

        default: [["anvil","anvil"],["pillow","pillow"]]  ->  ["20 kg","2 kg"]
  evenly loaded: [["anvil","pillow"],["anvil","pillow"]]  ->  ["11 kg","11 kg"]

           default: opens ["carton"], packaging cost 120
smallest box first: opens ["mailer"], packaging cost 190

None of these rules exists in the JSON request. Hand the same request to another
Packvium engine and you get the unrestricted answer -- which is exactly why a rule
everyone must obey belongs in the request as data, not in a class.
